  "worked_solution": "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{-2}\\frac{1}{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{-2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-3 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-3 \\\\ {\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12+10 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
